The '''G1 Climax 2026''' is the ongoing annual [[G1 Climax]] professional wrestling tournament produced by [[New Okaiken Pro-Wrestling|NOPW]], scheduled to run from September 5 to October 18, 2026. The tournament features 20 wrestlers divided into two blocks of 10, competing in a round-robin format across 18 tournament shows in 9 cities over 43 days, culminating in the G1 Final on October 18 at the [[Aizawa Dome]] in [[Aizawa]], [[Aizawa Prefecture]]. The winner of the tournament earns the right to challenge for the [[IGO Heavyweight Championship]] at [[Wrestling Summit]] on January 4, 2027.

The 2026 edition is notable for several firsts and major storylines: it is the first G1 Climax to feature the reigning IGO Heavyweight Champion as a tournament participant since 2019, with [[Leoni Masua]] entering as champion; it marks the G1 debut of [[Marcus Vance|Marcus "The Drill" Vance]], who enters the tournament as NOPW's hottest babyface following his betrayal by the [[Cannon Club]] at [[Island Invasion Tour 2026|Island Invasion]]; and it features the tournament debut of [[The Marauder]], the undefeated mystery powerhouse whose identity remains unknown. The tournament also marks the first G1 appearance of [[Honda Masanori]], the [[AOPW]] cross-promotional representative, and the first G1 for [[Yuto Ono]], the youngest entrant in the field at 24 years old.

The block draw, conducted live at [[NOPW Wednesday Episode 9]] on August 19 in [[Toyozawa]], placed Leoni and Vance in the same block — guaranteeing their first-ever one-on-one meeting in the round-robin — and placed [[Kengo Vaiahi|Kengo]] in the same block as both Leoni and [[Big Stan]], creating a three-way collision of family war, betrayal, and faction fracture within Block A.

