== Format ==

The G1 Climax is NOPW's most prestigious annual tournament. The format is a round-robin: 20 wrestlers are divided into two blocks of 10. Each wrestler faces every other wrestler in their block once, for a total of 9 matches per wrestler. Wins are worth 2 points, draws are worth 1 point, and losses are worth 0 points. The wrestler with the most points in each block advances to the G1 Final, where the two block winners face each other. The winner of the G1 Final earns the right to challenge for the IGO Heavyweight Championship at Wrestling Summit on January 4, 2027.

In the event of a tie on points, the tiebreaker is head-to-head result. If the head-to-head match was a draw, the tiebreaker is a decision by the tournament committee.

Matches have a 30-minute time limit during the block stage. The G1 Final has no time limit.

== Participants ==

The 20 participants were announced live at [[NOPW Wednesday Episode 9]] on August 19, 2026, with the block draw conducted the same night. The field includes three reigning champions — the IGO Heavyweight Champion, the IGO Intercontinental Champion, and the Strong Openweight Champion — as well as the World Television Champion and one cross-promotional representative from AOPW.

