=== Tournament headlines ===

* '''Day 1 (Okami):''' The champion's statement — Leoni def. Morita. Vance exposes the Marauder with the Ishida blueprint. Kengo steals one from Maeda. Kawada and Nakamura produce the match of the night. Stan overpowers Honda. ([[G1 Climax 2026 Day 1|Full results]])
* '''Day 2 (Okami):''' Block B opens. Jusuf submits Ishida in 8:56 — the fastest win of the tournament. KAZUKI wins his fourth straight. Taumafa vs. Ono ends in a passing-of-the-guard moment that did not pass. Takagi and Kuroki produce a strong-style classic. ([[G1 Climax 2026 Day 2|Full results]])
* '''Day 3 (Tokuyama):''' The first draw — Leoni and Honda go 30:00, the champion dropping points for the first time. Vance chops down Big Stan to take control of Block A. The Marauder no-sells Kengo's shortcuts. Maeda outlasts Nakamura in the match of the night. ([[G1 Climax 2026 Day 3|Full results]])
* '''Day 4 (Tokuyama):''' Jusuf's first loss — Takagi's Dragon lariat makes the truth-teller bump for the first time. Ishida's emotional rebound: the Ishida Lock submits Diallo. KAZUKI, Takagi, and Taumafa sit undefeated atop Block B at 4 points. ([[G1 Climax 2026 Day 4|Full results]])
* '''Day 5 (Aizawa):''' The family war — Leoni defeats Kengo in the champion's home city. Vance outlasts Kawada in the match of the night to stand alone at 3-0. And the injury costs him: Big Stan's knee gives out on the chokeslam lift, Nakamura takes the win, and the giant's tournament ends three days later in withdrawal. ([[G1 Climax 2026 Day 5|Full results]]; [[Big Stan knee injury (2026)|injury article]])
* '''Day 6 (Aizawa):''' KAZUKI def. Jusuf in 17:56 — and the truth-teller bumped for the Twin Star Press. Taumafa runs over Diallo to go 3-0. KAZUKI, Takagi, and Taumafa all stand perfect at 6 points. ([[G1 Climax 2026 Day 6|Full results]])
* '''Day 7 (Ogasawara):''' The first forfeit — Kawada collects the withdrawn Stan's points to a standing ovation. Vance pins Kengo clean in the betrayal match. Leoni def. Maeda, the dojo brothers' first G1 meeting. ([[G1 Climax 2026 Day 7|Full results]])
* '''Day 8 (Ogasawara):''' The Kuroshio reunion — KAZUKI def. Kuroki, then the bow of the brothers. And the Dragon bleeds: Ishida submits Takagi, the Ishida Lock's first giant-killing. KAZUKI and Taumafa stay perfect atop the block. ([[G1 Climax 2026 Day 8|Full results]])
* '''Day 9 (Naruto):''' The draw — Leoni and Vance go 30:00, both men standing at the bell, the Spear and the Drill Driver both kicked out of. Kawada hands the Marauder his first clean pin loss. ([[G1 Climax 2026 Day 9|Full results]])
* '''Day 10 (Naruto):''' The first collision of the undefeated three — KAZUKI def. Takagi in 21:12, the Dragon's second straight loss. Taumafa def. Jusuf in the champions' war. KAZUKI alone atop Block B at 5-0. ([[G1 Climax 2026 Day 10|Full results]])
* '''Day 11 (Tosa):''' Maeda solves the Marauder with speed — the second answer to the block's central question. Kawada def. Kengo; three men now sit within one point in Block A. Leoni collects the Stan forfeit. ([[G1 Climax 2026 Day 11|Full results]])
* '''Day 12 (Tosa):''' The family war — Taumafa catches the Twin Star Press and hands KAZUKI his first block loss since 2024; the block's top two now sit tied at 10. Ono passes the guard against Ishida. Jusuf and Takagi lead the chase at 8. ([[G1 Climax 2026 Day 12|Full results]])
* '''Day 13 (Anjo-Saikawa):''' The kickout match — the Marauder kicks out of the Spear of Fangatapu at 2.9 and leaves the main event legitimate; Leoni wins by a third Spear. Kawada def. Maeda — the Round 9 collision with the champion is set. Vance quietly goes to 6-0-1. ([[G1 Climax 2026 Day 13|Full results]])
* '''Day 14 (Anjo-Saikawa):''' The block flipped — Tadayoshi Ishida, written off at 3-3, makes KAZUKI tap to the Ishida Lock for the first time in two years. The top of Block B is now a four-man race: Taumafa 12, KAZUKI 12, Takagi 10, Jusuf 10. ([[G1 Climax 2026 Day 14|Full results]])
* '''Day 15 (Tsuda):''' Vance goes to 7-0-1 — one match from a perfect block, with only Morita remaining. Kawada def. Honda to set the Round 9 decider: Kawada vs. Leoni in Toyozawa. The Marauder collects the Stan forfeit to boos. ([[G1 Climax 2026 Day 15|Full results]])
* '''Day 16 (Tsuda):''' The block's marquee collision — Takagi hands Taumafa his second loss with the Dragon lariat in the main event. And the shock of the tournament: winless Diego Reyes makes KAZUKI tap to the Cobra Clutch. Three men at 12 with one night left. ([[G1 Climax 2026 Day 16|Full results]])
* '''Day 17 (Toyozawa):''' The draw that decided Block A — Leoni and Kawada go the full 30:00, both men standing at the bell, and the block goes to Vance, 8-0-1. The Workhorse wins without wrestling the night anyone will remember. ([[G1 Climax 2026 Day 17|Full results]])
* '''Day 18 (Toyozawa):''' The block ends in a tie — Taumafa def. Ishida to pull level with Takagi at 14 points, and Block B will be decided by the first playoff in G1 history. KAZUKI stops the slide but finishes in the 12-point pileup. ([[G1 Climax 2026 Day 18|Full results]])
* '''G1 Final (Aizawa Dome):''' The Workhorse speaks — [[Marcus Vance|Vance]] defeats [[Taumafa Vaiahi|Taumafa]] with the second Drill Driver at 27:44 to win the G1 Climax, then breaks nine matches of silence: ''Seventeen points. No words. One more man.'' The challenge is made: [[Wrestling Summit 2027|Wrestling Summit]], January 4, Toyozawa Dome. ([[G1 Climax 2026 Final|Full results]])
* '''Day 19 (Toyozawa):''' The playoff — Taumafa kicks out of the Dragon lariat and fells Takagi with the Samoan driver to win Block B. The Final is set: Vance vs. Taumafa, October 18, Aizawa Dome. ([[G1 Climax 2026 Day 19|Full results]])

=== Winner ===

The G1 Climax 2026 was won by [[Marcus Vance]], who defeated [[Taumafa Vaiahi|Taumafa]] in the Final at the [[Aizawa Dome]] on October 18 (second Drill Driver, 27:44) and challenged [[Leoni Masua]] for the [[IGO Heavyweight Championship]] at [[Wrestling Summit 2027|Wrestling Summit]]. ([[G1 Climax 2026 Final|Full results]])

